course: dictionary
lesson: 15716
title: Traceable: following a trail back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Traceable means able to be found or followed back to where it started. The root word is trace, a mark or sign that something has been there. Footprints in mud are traceable: you can follow them back to the person who made them.
explain: «The eggs in the shop are fully traceable to the farm they came from.» The word fully tells you the path is complete: you can follow every step from the shop back to the farm. Ask yourself: can someone follow this back to its start? If yes, it is traceable.
explain: The word also works in other subjects. «The phone calls were easily traceable, so the police could find where they began.» In history, «The illness was traceable to dirty water» means people found its cause. Traceable to means the start, or cause, can be found.
explain: There is one rare meaning: a picture that is traceable can be copied by drawing over it, like tracing a map on thin paper. Because this meaning is rare, the first meaning is the one you will meet most often.
fact: Traceable means able to be found or followed back to where it started.
fact: Traceable food can be followed back to the farm it came from.
fact: «Traceable to» means a cause can be found.
fact: Money, emails and phone calls may be traceable.
fact: Rare meaning: a picture that can be copied by drawing over it is traceable.
exercise: «The eggs in the shop are fully traceable to the farm.» What does traceable mean here? | Very cheap | Kept cold in a fridge | *Able to be followed back to where it started | Easy to see from far away
exercise: «The phone calls were easily ___, so the police could find where they began.» Which word fits the gap? | ancient | hungry | *traceable | sunny
exercise: «The illness was traceable to dirty water.» What does traceable to mean here? | It spreads very fast | *The cause can be found | It is kept in the water only | It is very quiet
test: Ben says traceable means the same as visible. Why is he wrong? | Traceable means something is always dirty | Traceable means you can see something from far away | *Traceable means you can follow something back to its start, not just see it | Traceable means something is very cheap
test: «Mia drew over the map on thin paper, because the picture was traceable.» What does traceable mean in this sentence? | Very large and heavy | Hidden under the paper | Able to be followed back to where it started | *Able to be copied by drawing over it
exam: «The bread was fully traceable, so the shop could show which mill made the flour.» What does traceable mean here? | Hard to chew | Very hot from the oven | *Able to be followed back to where it started | Covered in seeds
